GIT_COMMIT ->
Short git commit hash of the server binary.

SPECTATOR ->
Implementation-defined signed integer value for the spectator team.

PID_BROADCAST ->
Implementation-defined signed integer broadcast pid that refers to all connected players.

MAX_PLAYERS ->
The most player IDs the implementation and protocol can handle at once. I.e., usually 32.
Valid player IDs are integers in the range of 0 to MAX_PLAYERS&minus;1 inclusive.

ENET_PORT ->
UDP port the server is listening for <a rel=noreferrer href=http://sauerbraten.org/enet/>ENet</a> connections on.

CULL_PERSONALITY_VOXLAP ->
Voxlap-type cull personality used with set_cull_personality().

CULL_PERSONALITY_OPENSPADES ->
OpenSpades-type cull personality used with set_cull_personality().

QUIRK_INFLOOR ->
Handles <var>pos</var>.z of the spawn player packet with no offset instead of &minus;2.

QUIRK_NOSHORTPLAYER ->
The short player data packet is not used; change team and change gun are used separately instead.

QUIRK_SCREWED_DISCONNECT_DATA ->
``Too many connections'' takes the place of disconnect code 2, which is normally ``Kicked''.

QUIRK_OS_CP437 ->
OpenSpades' variant of CP-437 is used instead of Voxlap's variant.

QUIRK_UTF8 ->
Sent and received strings may begin with a <code>&apos;\xff&apos;</code> byte and be followed by valid
UTF-8, in which case that UTF-8 is used directly instead of the whole thing (including
<code>&apos;\xff&apos;</code> being decoded as CP-437.

QUIRK_ASCII ->
The printable subset of ASCII (including the space) is used in place of sent and received CP-437.
Bytes not present in that subset are handled as if they weren't present to begin with.

QUIRK_OS_BACTION_CULL ->
Sent destroying block action packets do not process gravity on nonsolid voxels within the destroyed shape;
behaves like CULL_PERSONALITY_OPENSPADES instead of CULL_PERSONALITY_VOXLAP.

QUIRK_UTF8_COLOR_IMG ->
The gray UTF-8 color moves from <code>&apos;\x07&apos;</code> to <code>&apos;\x08&apos;</code>;
<code>&apos;\x07&apos;</code> is now used to display specific images inline with text when
coupled with a lowercase letter immediately after it.

QUIRK_INSKY ->
Handles <var>pos</var>.z of the spawn player packet with an offset of &minus;2.4 instead of &minus;2.
